What is really driving e-commerce revenue — products, payment methods, customers, or devices?

I recently completed an E-commerce Orders Analysis project using Power BI, where I analyzed order and revenue data for Summer 2024–2025 to understand sales performance and identify patterns that could support better business decisions.

🔍 Business Questions I explored:

• Which product categories contribute the most to total revenue?
• How does revenue change over time?
• Which payment methods generate the highest revenue?
• Which countries contribute most to sales?
• Are customers purchasing more through mobile, desktop, or tablet?
• What is the overall volume of delivered and returned orders?

📈 Key Metrics

Total Revenue: 10.22M
Male Customers: 25K
Female Customers: 25K
Mobile Orders: 31K
Delivered Orders: 42K
Returned Orders: 4K

💡 What I analyzed

The dashboard provides a consolidated view of:

🔹 Revenue trends by month and year
🔹 Revenue by product category
🔹 Revenue by payment method
🔹 Revenue by country
🔹 Revenue by device
🔹 Order status and customer segments

